course: dictionary
lesson: 1027
title: Words about betting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bookmaker is a business that takes bets. A bet is when someone puts money on what they think will happen, such as which horse will win a race. The bookmaker keeps the bets and pays out money to the people who guessed right.
explain: «Gambling is betting money on something uncertain; a bookmaker is a business that takes bets, and on average players lose more than they win.» The clue is uncertain, which means you cannot know the result for sure. So gambling is risky, and a bookmaker is part of it.
explain: Bookmaker has a rare second meaning: a person who makes or prints books. In a money lesson, the betting meaning is the one that fits. Use the words around the word to decide which meaning is right.
fact: A bookmaker is a person or company that takes bets on horse races, football matches and other events.
fact: «Bookie» is a short, everyday name for a bookmaker.
fact: In maths, the odds a bookmaker gives are linked to probability, which is how likely something is to happen.
fact: Gambling is only for adults: the age limit is 18 in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, and it varies in the USA and Canada.
fact: On average, players lose more than they win, so gambling can lead to losing money.
exercise: «Gambling is betting money on something uncertain; a bookmaker is a business that takes bets.» What does a bookmaker do? | Makes books and prints them for schools | *Takes bets and pays out to people who win | Sells sweets at the football match | Runs the buses to the races
exercise: What is another everyday name for a bookmaker? | Banker | Printer | Racer | *Bookie
exercise: Who is gambling and betting meant for? | Children of any age | *Adults only | Anyone who has a pet | Only pupils at school
test: In maths, the odds a bookmaker gives link to which idea? | Measuring length | *Probability | Multiplication tables | Reading clocks
test: What can gambling lead to? | Always winning | *Losing money | Getting free money from school | Growing taller
exam: Which sentence uses bookmaker in its rare meaning? | The bookmaker paid out when the horse won | The bookmaker took my bet on the race | The bookmaker is open on Saturday | *A bookmaker prints and binds the books for the library
